WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.468
-You guys, we have got
a great show tonight,

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.903
one you definitely
would want to miss --

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.738
I mean wouldn't want to miss.
Would --

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.173
Sorry, would -- You would --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:10.376
You wouldn't want it --
You would -- I meant to say --

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:14.046
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:15.415
You guys hear about this?
-Ugh.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.417
-After all the backlash
to his press conference

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.519
with Vladimir Putin,
President Trump said that

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.454
the whole thing
was a big misunderstanding

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:24.557
because he said the word "would"
when he meant to say "wouldn't."

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.159
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:28.727
The saddest part
of that explanation is that

00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:30.496
it took him 24 hours
to come up with it.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:33.399
It's like, "That's the --
That's what happened?"

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:34.901
"Oh, yeah, definitely."

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.137
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.572
But Trump says
he now accepts U.S. intelligence

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.707
that Russia interfered
with our election.

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.776
Trump was like,
"After 18 months as president,

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:46.512
I've decided
to try something totally new --

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:47.613
intelligence."

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:49.982
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:52.885
"I'm gonna try it. I'm gonna
try some intelligence."

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:54.586
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.586 --> 00:00:56.790
That's right, Trump's really
in damage-control mode,

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.358
and the best excuse
he came up with

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.926
was he said "would"
instead of "wouldn't."

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.361
The whole thing
sounded kind of crazy.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.363
But maybe that's just because
Trump's the one who said it I --

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.464
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.532
I wonder if it
would sound less crazy

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.200
coming out of
someone else's mouth?

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.734
Does anybody here
want to give it a shot?

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.236
Does anyone want to read
what the President said,

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.605
word for word,
see if it makes any more sense?

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:13.873
♪♪

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.007
Who's over here?
Yeah.

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:17.310
Come on.
Who wants to do it?

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.045
Come on.
No one's raising their hand?

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.147
Oh, hey, yeah, yeah.
Go try, yeah, try.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.915
We'll see, we'll see.
Yeah, try it.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:24.017
Come on.
-Follow you?

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.718
-Yeah, yeah, follow me.
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.654
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:30.289
There you go, take that.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:32.191
Yeah, yeah, it's fantastic.
It's very easy.

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:33.726
Yeah, come here, yeah.
-Okay.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.161
-Here you go.
Take that microphone there.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.295
You just hit
the monologue mark here.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:37.430
-I'm terrible
at public speaking.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.564
-What is your name?
-I'm Bridget.

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:39.665
-Bridget?
Okay, good.

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:40.700
And you're terrible at pub--
perfect.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.868
-I'm terrible.
-Perfect.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.336
Okay, this will go great.
All right.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:46.606
These are the exact words of the
President of the United States.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.874
Let's see if they sound any
less crazy when you say them.

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:50.310
Take it away, Bridget.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.812
-It should've been obvious.
I thought it would be obvious.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.615
But, I would like to clarify,
just in case it wasn't.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.449
In a key sentence in my remarks,

00:01:57.449 --> 00:02:00.019
I said the word "would"
instead of "wouldn't."

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.689
The sentence should've been,
"I don't see any reason why

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.124
I wouldn't,
or why it wouldn't be Russia."

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:06.725
So, just to repeat,

00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:09.328
I said the word "would"
instead of "wouldn't."

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:11.397
-Okay.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.032
-There's more?
This side?

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.400
-Yeah.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.968
-And the sentence
should have been --

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.270
And I thought it would be
maybe a little bit unclear,

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.607
on the transcript,
or unclear on the actual video.

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.208
The sentence should have been

00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:26.278
"I don't see any reason
why it wouldn't be Russia."

00:02:26.278 --> 00:02:28.982
Sort of a double-negative.
So can you put that in?

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.017
And I think
that probably clarifies things

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.386
pretty good by itself.
-That's -- hey!

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.787
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.022
♪♪

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.491
Nailed it!
Actually, much better!

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.593
You can take that with you.
Thank you, Bridget, yeah.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.795
Hey, not bad.
That's fantastic.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.931
Bridget, thank you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.232
♪♪

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.767
Actually -- Actually,
it does make more sense.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.102
-Oh, now I get it!
Yeah.

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:51.737
-Yeah, now it makes more sense
that Bridget says it.

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.106
Yeah, sure.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.808
Good job, pal.
You guys see this?

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.844
While he spoke to reporters,
people could see

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.545
the handwritten notes
that he was reading,

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:02.582
and on his sheet, he spelled
"collusion" with one L.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.950
This is real.
Take a look.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.451
This is a real photo.
Look at that.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.052
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.052 --> 00:03:09.121
When his staff told him
that collusion has two L's,

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:12.125
he was like, "Got it --
two L's, just like 'Donalld.'"

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.158
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.158 --> 00:03:14.627
"Two L's."

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.797
D-D-D-D-O...

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.899
At his Cabinet meeting today,
Trump pushed back

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:22.235
against everyone who thinks that
he's too close to Russia.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.536
Check out what he said.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.638
-We're doing very well.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.942
Probably as well as anybody
has ever done with Russia.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:32.845
And there's been no President
ever as tough

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.780
as I have been on Russia.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.816
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:39.886
He's like, "I've been tougher
than all the presidents.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:43.021
Harrison Ford, Martin Sheen,
Alec Baldwin."

00:03:43.021 --> 00:03:44.924
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:48.894
"That guy
from the Allstate commercials."

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:51.297
Get this -- it just came out
that Trump spends more money

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:54.500
on Facebook ads
than any other politician.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.001
When he heard about it,
Putin was like,

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:58.804
"Hey, Donald can spend allowance
however he wants."

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:00.606
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:04.277
"He can do
whatever he wants with it."

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.746
Some more political news --
I read that Starbucks founder

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:10.082
Howard Schultz might run
for President in 2020.

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:11.384
[ Cheers ]
Yeah.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.819
He seems pretty serious
about it, too.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:15.587
In fact, he's already got some
campaign slogans picked out.

00:04:15.587 --> 00:04:17.590
For instance, there's,
"Howard Schultz --

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.958
Cooler than the center of
a Starbucks breakfast sandwich."

00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:22.094
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:23.829
"Mm.

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.631
Can you put this back in
for 20 seconds?"

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:26.732
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.200
Next up, there's,
"Howard Schultz --

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.103
One nation, understaffed
during peak hours."

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:34.106
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:36.175
And finally, there's,
"Howard Schultz --

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.811
Make Americano great again."

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:39.979
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:43.683
A venti Americano.

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.851
Listen to this, you guys --

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.652
the World Airlines Awards
was just announced,

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:49.155
and Delta was named
the top U.S. airline.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.424
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.892
They would have
accepted the award,

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:55.561
but their flight to the ceremony
was delayed six hours

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.164
and then canceled.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:00.933
Eh, you get them next year.

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.702
This is very interesting.
Did you see this?

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.870
The FDA might start
to limit which drinks

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.373
can call themselves milk.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.841
Which means that
all the companies

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:11.910
that make milk alternatives,
like soy milk, almond milk,

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.246
stuff like that,
they're all scrambling

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.980
to come up with new names.
-Wow.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.449
-I don't know
if they're good or not,

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.517
but let's just check out what
some of them are considering.

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:21.454
For instance, almond milk
will now be called Nut Juice.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:23.055
-Really?
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:25.525
-Yeah.
-Really?

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:28.127
That doesn't seem like
a good idea at all.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.761
-I think it's good.
-That seems awful.

00:05:29.761 --> 00:05:31.230
-I think
it clarifies everything.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.033
Next up, peanut milk
will be called Liquid Pea.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.835
-Okay.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:39.238
-Lastly, hemp milk
will now be called Bong Water.

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.540
So if you just --
Just so you know that.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:45.678
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:47.145
And finally,
here's a local story.

00:05:47.145 --> 00:05:49.815
A man in New York City just set
a Guinness World Record,

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:51.083
and the local news
was there to cover it.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.485
Check out what he did.

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.787
-Ashrita Furman set a new record

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:58.691
for slicing the most watermelon
in half on his own stomach

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.826
in one minute.
It's a very specific --

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:02.762
-Oh, my.
-Yeah, thing that he did.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:04.730
He says he's relieved
he did not kill himself.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:12.771
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.771 --> 00:06:14.707
-He beat the previous record,
which was zero.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.041
No one wants to do that.

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:18.211
We have a great show tonight!
Give it up for The Roots!

